	4. Tomcat and java web applications
		4.1 Packaged apps are moved to the webapps directory. If the server is running it automatically starts the application.
	5. Gunicorn and python web applications
		5.1 Requirements are installed with "pip install -r requirements.txt" command line
		5.2 "gunicorn app:app" is used to start the application
		5.3 If the name of the main application file is app, then configure app.py file for ip and port definitions.
	6. pm2, nodejs and express
		6.1 To install requirements, use npm install. With this commands npm will look into the package.json file's spesific section then take instructions to continue installing the requirements.
		6.2 Look at the package.json file, if there are scripts to be executed to prepare the application for a spesific context then take that into account.
			- Start the app with "npm run start"
			- If a spesific mode is to be started use "npm run start <mode_name"
		6.3 To start the app normally, use "node app.js"
		6.4 To use pm2 to manage the application use "pm2 start app.js"
			- To spawn multiple instances, "pm2 start app.js -i <4>"		


